#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../templates:1001
msgid "Default Node.js version to install:"
msgstr ""

#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../templates:1001
msgid ""
"update-node-alternatives can download a Node.js version through the bundled "
"nvm and register it as the system-wide alternative right after the package "
"is configured."
msgstr ""

#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../templates:1001
msgid ""
" - \"latest LTS\" installs the most recent Long-Term Support release;\n"
" - \"latest\" installs the most recent Node.js release;\n"
" - \"none\" leaves the system without a Node.js version (the default);\n"
" - \"custom\" lets you type a specific version string (e.g. v22.14.0,\n"
"   lts/jod, 20)."
msgstr ""

#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../templates:1001
msgid ""
"Choosing \"none\" is always safe: you can install or change the active "
"version later with `update-node-alternatives --install <version>`."
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../templates:2001
msgid "Custom Node.js version to install:"
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../templates:2001
msgid ""
"Type the Node.js version string to install. Anything accepted by `update-"
"node-alternatives --install` (and ultimately by nvm) works: a major number "
"(22), a full version (v22.14.0), or an alias (lts/jod, lts/*, node)."
msgstr ""

#. Type: boolean
#. Description
#: ../templates:3001
msgid "Remove all installed Node.js versions on apt purge?"
msgstr ""

#. Type: boolean
#. Description
#: ../templates:3001
msgid ""
"update-node-alternatives stores Node.js versions under /usr/local/share/"
"nvm/, outside dpkg's tree. By default `apt purge` leaves that store "
"untouched."
msgstr ""

#. Type: boolean
#. Description
#: ../templates:3001
msgid ""
"When enabled, `apt purge` will also delete /usr/local/share/nvm/, along with "
"every Node.js version installed through this package. The choice is recorded "
"now and re-confirmed at purge time."
msgstr ""
